# Generated, byte-compared artifacts.
#
# CI asserts that `npm run seed` and `npm run seed:anomalies` regenerate these
# files byte-identically. A formatter that rewrote them would make the emitter
# and the repo disagree forever, and the determinism gate would fail on a
# whitespace change rather than on a real one. The emitter owns their bytes.
seed/content/
seed/telemetry-anomalies.json

# Lockfiles are npm's output, not ours.
package-lock.json
worker/package-lock.json
app/package-lock.json

# Binary / generated assets.
docs/assets/
worker/public/assets/

# The pitch deck is assembled outside the repo and byte-compared: its bite-times
# table must equal renderBiteTimes() exactly (tests/landing.test.js). A
# formatter that reflowed that markup would break the equality on whitespace.
worker/public/pitch/

# Judge-facing prose. Prettier's Markdown printer pads table cells to the width
# of the widest row (turning a readable table into 250-character lines) and
# rewrites `*emphasis*` to `_emphasis_`. Both make the source of the documents a
# judge actually reads worse, and neither catches a defect. Code is formatted;
# prose is written.
*.md

node_modules/
coverage/
.wrangler/
.expo/
dist/
